cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Subjective-Ride-Comfort-ML: research code for predicting subjective ride comfort with machine learning"
abstract: >-
  Jupyter notebook used in the study "Machine Learning Techniques for Subjective Ride Comfort
  Performance Prediction in Automotive Suspensions": exploratory analysis, Pearson correlation,
  PCA and multi-output and single-output regression and classification models that relate
  objective vehicle-dynamics metrics from simulator runs to subjective ride-comfort ratings.
authors:
